Dr. Jonathan Crane, played by Cillian Murphy.

11
00:45:17,647 --> 00:45:23,647
Batman Begins is a 2005 superhero film based on the DC Comics character Batman.

12
00:49:24,705 --> 00:49:30,705
Directed by Christopher Nolan, who co-wrote the screenplay with David S.

13
00:53:31,764 --> 00:53:37,764
Goyer, the film stars Christian Bale as Bruce Wayne / Batman, with Michael Caine, Liam Neeson, Katie Holmes, Gary
Oldman, Cillian Murphy, Tom Wilkinson, Rutger Hauer, Ken Watanabe, and Morgan Freeman in supporting roles.

14
00:57:38,823 --> 00:57:44,823
The film reboots the Batman film series, telling the origin story of Bruce Wayne from the death of his parents to his journey to
become Batman and his fight to stop Ra's al Ghul (Neeson) and the Scarecrow (Murphy) from plunging Gotham City into chaos.

15
01:01:45,882 --> 01:01:51,882
After Batman & Robin (1997) was panned by critics and
underperformed at the box office, Warner Bros.

16
01:05:52,941 --> 01:05:58,941
Pictures cancelled future Batman films, including Joel
Schumacher's planned Batman Unchained.

17
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Between 1998 and 2003, several filmmakers collaborated with Warner Bros.

18
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
in attempting to reboot the franchise.

19
01:18:14,117 --> 01:18:20,117
After the studio rejected a Batman origin story reboot Joss
Whedon pitched in December 2002, Warner Bros.

20
01:22:21,176 --> 01:22:27,176
hired Nolan in January 2003 to direct a new film.

21
01:26:28,235 --> 01:26:34,235
Nolan and Goyer began development on the film in early 2003.

22
01:30:35,294 --> 01:30:41,294
Aiming for a darker, more realistic tone compared to the previous films, a primary goal for their vision was to engage
the audience's emotional investment in both the Batman and Bruce Wayne identities of the lead character.

23
01:34:42,352 --> 01:34:48,352
The film, which was principally shot in the United Kingdom, Iceland and Chicago, relied heavily on traditional stunts and
miniature effects, with computer-generated imagery being used in a minimal capacity compared to other action films.

24
01:38:49,411 --> 01:38:55,411
Comic book storylines such as The Man Who Falls, Batman: Year One,
and Batman: The Long Halloween served as inspiration.

25
01:42:56,470 --> 01:43:02,470
Expectations for Batman Begins ranged from moderate to low, which originated from the poor reception
of Batman & Robin that was credited with stalling the Batman film series in 1997.

26
01:47:03,529 --> 01:47:09,529
After premiering in Tokyo on May 31, 2005, the film was
released in the United States on June 15.

27
01:51:10,588 --> 01:51:16,588
It was a critical and commercial success, grossing over $371.9 million worldwide against a $150 million budget, becoming the ninth
highest-grossing film of 2005, and was the second highest grossing Batman film at the time of its release, behind Tim Burton's Batman (1989).

28
01:55:17,647 --> 01:55:23,647
Receiving a nomination for the Academy Award for Best Cinematography, the film elevated
Bale to leading man status while it made Nolan a high-profile director.

29
01:59:24,705 --> 01:59:30,705
Since its release, Batman Begins has often been cited as one
of the most influential films of the 2000s.

30
02:03:31,764 --> 02:03:37,764
The film helped popularize the term reboot in Hollywood, inspiring studios and
filmmakers to revive franchises with realistic and serious tones.

31
02:07:38,823 --> 02:07:44,823
It was followed by The Dark Knight (2008) and The Dark Knight Rises (2012),
with the three films constituting The Dark Knight trilogy.

32
02:11:45,882 --> 02:11:51,882
The film explores themes of martial arts, undercover, loss of
loved one, secret identity, crime fighter.

33
02:15:52,941 --> 02:15:58,941
The tone is emotional.
